      "notes": "KP government women-only Pink Bus (not a private service); suspended in 2019. Government/UNOPS women-only Pink Bus using buses donated by Japan, not a private route. The stop sequence comes from Dawn 2018, before launch. Dawn Images 2019 confirms both endpoints, the 18 km length, 7 buses and 15 UNOPS-built solar-lit stops, so not every named point may have had a built shelter. Launched around April-May 2019 and suspended a few months later. Pakistan Gender News (2021-02) says KP decided to shut it because no operator bid. Treat as defunct or historical, like the withdrawn Peshawar wagon route. Fare not stated for Abbottabad. The route runs along the main Abbottabad corridor (Mansehra Road/Supply/Mandian) that Suzukis also serve."
